From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net airoha keep polling an rx ring that could not be refilled

airoha_qdma_fill_rx_queue() stops at the first failed page_pool
allocation and the ring is only refilled from the RX NAPI poll.  Under
memory pressure a ring can run down to no buffer at all: the QDMA then
drops every frame for it, raises no RX done interrupt, the poll is never
scheduled again and the ring stays dead until the driver is reloaded.
Seen as a possibility in review, not on hardware.

When the poll ends with an empty ring, return the full budget so NAPI
polls again and the refill is retried; the frames that come meanwhile
are lost as before, but the ring recovers once memory is back.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1197,6 +1197,15 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_napi_poll(stru
 		done += cur;
 	} while (cur && done < budget);
 
+	/*
+	 * Not a single buffer could be given back to the ring (page_pool
+	 * out of memory): the QDMA has nowhere to put a frame, so no RX
+	 * interrupt will come to schedule the refill.  Stay scheduled, the
+	 * next poll tries again.
+	 */
+	if (!q->queued)
+		return budget;
+
 	if (done < budget && napi_complete(napi)) {
 		struct airoha_qdma *qdma = q->qdma;
 		int i, qid = q - &qdma->q_rx[0];
